k0s-cilium reboot-remote: after remote1 is SIGKILLed and returns, the
remote1<->remote2 pairs alone never recover: the convergence gate
waited its full 420s and gave up on both directions, while all 108
other checks (remote<->site included) passed. cp-dies on the same row
passed. kubeadm-cilium passed this identical row, so the distribution
is the variable, not the network.

The remote<->remote leg is the only one that crosses cloud to cloud
directly, peer to peer over public addresses rather than through a
site endpoint, and the only one a remote bootstrap list cannot
describe: remote1 was rendered before remote2 existed, so after a
reboot that path exists only if the adoption cache is re-read.
